These functions work by copying the contents of the left-hand operand into temp, removing any occurrences of the substring specified by the right-hand operand during the process. The resulting StrType object is returned. Understand that neither operand is modified by the process. The StrType class allows substring subtractions like these:

StrType x("I like C++"), y("like");
StrType z;
z = x - y; // z will contain "I C++"
z = x - "C++"; // z will contain "I like "
// multiple occurrences are removed
z = "ABCDABCD";
x = z -"A"; // x contains "BCDBCD"

